<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Is it better to fold or roll clothes to save space?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Both work, and the best way to fold clothes to save space depends on where they go. In a drawer, file folding is usually tidier because the pieces keep their shape and stand upright. Rolling suits stretchy fabrics, pajamas and suitcases, where rolls fill gaps and stay put. Many people use both: file folds for shirts and jeans, rolls for leggings and underwear.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">What is the KonMari folding method?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The KonMari method, from organizing consultant Marie Kondo, folds each garment into a small, firm rectangle that stands on its edge. You store the pieces upright in rows so you can see everything in the drawer at once.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How do you fold clothes to save space in drawers?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The file fold is the simplest option. Fold each item into a rectangle about as tall as the drawer, minus about 1 in (2–3 cm), and file it upright from back to front. Use dividers or small boxes to keep rows straight, and keep the most-worn items at the front.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How do I fold clothes to fit more in a suitcase?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Roll soft items tightly with the ranger roll, file fold shirts into packing cubes, and use the gaps inside shoes for socks. Put heavier items at the wheel end of the case so it stays balanced.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Final Thoughts</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Once you know how to fold clothes to save space, every drawer becomes easier to use. Start with T-shirts, usually the biggest category in a dresser, then move on to jeans, socks and towels. Within a weekend your dresser will hold more and look calmer, and folding laundry will take less time because every piece has a clear place to go.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If your laundry room is where the folding happens, our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/small-laundry-room-ideas/">small laundry room ideas</a> include space-saving folding counters and fold-down surfaces. And if you are short on closet space too, our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/small-walk-in-closet-ideas/">small walk-in closet ideas</a> are a good next read.</p>



